  "worked_solution": "The angles that the ray makes with the positive $x$-axis is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\theta =arctan\\,(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the ray lies in the first quadrant, its polar equation is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$",
